<TeXmacs|2.1.4>

<style|<tuple|tmdoc|english>>

<\body>
  <tmdoc-title|Plug-ins, collaboration and remote services>

  These chapters describe how <TeXmacs> talks to other programs and to other
  <TeXmacs> instances: the sessions, pipes and dynamic libraries through
  which plug-ins are connected, and the client/server system used for
  shared documents, live collaborative editing, remote file systems and
  versioning.

  How to <em|write> a plug-in is explained in <hlink|the <TeXmacs> plug-in
  system|../plugin/plugins.en.tm> and in <hlink|interfacing <TeXmacs> with
  other programs|../interface/interface.en.tm>; setting up a server is
  explained in <hlink|setting up a <TeXmacs>
  server|../../main/remote/man-server.en.tm>.

  <\traverse>
    <branch|The plug-in machinery|plugins.en.tm>

    <branch|Collaboration, remote servers and versioning|collaboration.en.tm>
  </traverse>

